<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Ch07_P04_Transfer_The_Method</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>In the example above, \(f(k+1) = f(k) + \left(3 \times 4^k + 15\right)\), and a second induction (the lemma) showed that \(3 \times 4^k + 15\) is always a multiple of 9. Use the same method for</p>
<p>\[g(n) = {@aa@}^n + {@cc@}n - 1,\]</p>
<p>which is a multiple of {@dd@} for every positive integer \(n\).</p>
<ol class="tb-parts">
<li><p>Find \(h(k)\) such that \(g(k+1) = g(k) + h(k)\).</p>
<div>\(h(k) =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div></li>
<li><p>The lemma you would need says that \(h(j)\) is a multiple of {@dd@} for every positive integer \(j\). Its induction step writes \(h(t+1) = {@aa@} \times h(t) - N\), where \(N\) is a number. Find \(N\).</p>
<div>\(N =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div></li>
</ol>]]></text></questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The method needs a lemma because \(g(k+1) - g(k)\) still contains a power of {@aa@}, so it needs an induction of its own.</p>
<ol class="tb-parts">
<li><p>Work out \(g(k+1) - g(k)\) term by term. Since \({@aa@}^{k+1} = {@aa@} \times {@aa@}^k\), we have \({@aa@}^{k+1} - {@aa@}^k = {@aa-1@} \times {@aa@}^k\), and \({@cc@}(k+1) - {@cc@}k = {@cc@}\). So</p>
<p>\[h(k) = {@aa-1@} \times {@aa@}^k + {@cc@}.\]</p></li>
<li><p>The lemma's base case is \(h(1) = {@aa-1@} \times {@aa@} + {@cc@} = {@h1@} = {@dd@} \times {@h1q@}\). For its induction step, \({@aa@} \times h(t) = {@aa-1@} \times {@aa@}^{t+1} + {@dg3@}\), while \(h(t+1) = {@aa-1@} \times {@aa@}^{t+1} + {@cc@}\). So</p>
<p>\[h(t+1) = {@aa@} \times h(t) - {@ta2@},\]</p>
<p>and \(N = {@ta2@} = {@dd@} \times {@qq@}\), a multiple of {@dd@}. If \(h(t) = {@dd@}s\) for some integer \(s\), then \(h(t+1) = {@aa@} \times {@dd@}s - {@ta2@} = {@dd@}\left({@aa@}s - {@qq@}\right)\), which is a multiple of {@dd@}.</p>
<p>Then, as in the example, if \(g(k) = {@dd@}m\), the lemma with \(j = k\) gives \(h(k) = {@dd@}s\), and \(g(k+1) = {@dd@}m + {@dd@}s = {@dd@}(m + s)\).</p></li>
</ol>]]></text></generalfeedback>
